# Environment overrides for the :superintelligence module.
#
# Copy to .env in this directory and edit, or load straight into a shell. Nothing here is required: with no
# .env and no SPD_* variables the run uses the compiled defaults, which are exactly the values in
# superintelligence.properties beside this file. That is what makes adding a file a non-event.
#
# It sits here rather than at the repository root because it configures this module and nothing else,
# and a configuration file that has to be found by walking up two directories is a configuration file
# nobody edits.
#
# RESOLUTION ORDER, lowest priority first:
#   1. the compiled defaults in EnvConfig and PpoHyperparameters
#   2. superintelligence.properties
#   3. these SPD_* variables
#   4. command-line flags, which override everything
#
# The name of a key is the key itself, upper-cased, with dots replaced by underscores and prefixed
# SPD_. reward.depth_reward -> SPD_REWARD_DEPTH_REWARD. Every key in the properties file has one; the
# list below is the reward half, which is what a run is usually tuned on.
#
# A value that cannot be read is REFUSED rather than defaulted, and an unknown key warns naming
# itself. A configuration that is not the one you asked for is worse than one that declines to load.
#
# .env is not read by the JVM. Load it first, eg.
#   pwsh:  Get-Content .env | Where-Object { $_ -match '=' } | ForEach-Object { $k,$v = $_ -split '=',2; Set-Item -Path "env:$($k.Trim())" -Value $v.Trim() }
#   bash:  set -a; . ./.env; set +a

# --- reward: the objective --------------------------------------------------
#
# Which terms are allowed to pay at all. `default` pays every term. `depth_only` silences every term
# except reaching a new floor and winning, and keeps only four negatives: the per-turn cost, the charge
# for a step the engine resolved for free, running out of turns, dying and stalling.
#
# TEMPORARY OVERRIDE - nothing below is re-priced when it is on, terms are silenced - so `default`
# restores the full reward function. It exists because a run can score well under the full function
# without ever leaving floor 1, which makes progress indistinguishable from exploration. `rewardcheck`
# asserts both directions of the property.
SPD_REWARD_PROFILE=default
#
# THE NUMBER TO CHANGE FIRST when depth does not move. A regular floor holds several hundred
# walkable tiles, so exploration alone can bank more than descending pays, and every run so far has
# wandered rather than taken the stairs. The ratio between this and explore_reward is the objective.
SPD_REWARD_DEPTH_REWARD=1800.0

# Small on purpose: a hint toward moving, not a reason to prefer moving to arriving.
SPD_REWARD_EXPLORE_REWARD=0.05

# Shaped reward for closing the gap to the stairs: gamma*Phi(s') - Phi(s), Phi the negative
# breadth-first distance. Telescopes over an episode, so a round trip pays nothing and only arriving
# pays. 0 measures what it was worth.
SPD_REWARD_STAIR_POTENTIAL_WEIGHT=2.0

# Constant per-turn cost. Only matters relative to the two above.
SPD_REWARD_TURN_COST=1.0

# --- reward: terminal outcomes ---------------------------------------------
#
# Ordered: giving up is worse than dying, dying is worse than running out of a floor, and running out
# of a floor is worse than clearing one. Any inversion among them is a strategy, and the agent will
# find it. Asserted by `rewardcheck`.
SPD_REWARD_STALL_PENALTY=3000.0
SPD_REWARD_DEATH_PENALTY=2500.0
SPD_REWARD_TURN_LIMIT_PENALTY=2000.0
SPD_REWARD_VICTORY_REWARD=60000.0

# --- reward: combat ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# KILL is read from Statistics.enemiesSlain, the engine's own counter. It existed and never fired,
# so fighting was worth nothing while being hit cost something. Sized against damage_penalty: a floor-1
# rat is ~8 HP and a melee kill trades about half, so melee is break-even and the profitable kill is the
# sneak.
SPD_REWARD_KILL_REWARD=150.0

# Read from Statistics.sneakAttacks, which Mob.defenseProc increments exactly when Mob.surprisedBy
# holds - the mob has not seen the hero. Deliberately the largest combat payout, because it is the only
# outcome that COSTS THE HERO NOTHING: Mob.surprisedBy skips the defender's defence skill outright, so
# the hit takes far more off the same health pool and none comes back.
#
# Fighting has to be worth doing and the only way it is worth doing is to not be hit. Paying both
# outcomes the same teaches trading blows, and trading blows is what the recorded deaths look like.
SPD_REWARD_SNEAK_ATTACK_REWARD=300.0

# SIZED AGAINST death_penalty, not picked. damage_penalty x 20 is what losing a full floor-1 health bar
# costs: 50, half a death. At the old 0.25 it was 5 - five per cent - and a run dying 100% of its
# episodes returned the same terminal every time, so there was no gradient to learn from at all.
#
# The relationship is the property, and it binds the combat payouts too: kill_reward must cover what a
# fight costs. Halving one without the others unbalances it - at 5.0 with kill_reward 3.0, killing a rat
# cost 40 and paid 3, a net -37 to fight.
#
# Known weakness: linear per-HP is depth-dependent, because the bar grows. Recorded, not designed away.
SPD_REWARD_DAMAGE_PENALTY=40.0

# --- reward: free actions ---------------------------------------------------
#
# Equipping and unequipping spend no engine time at all - WndUseItem.onClick calls item.execute and
# returns - so they are free in the real game too, and a policy found the loop. Charged per step
# rather than handled by the stall guard, because the guard decides when an episode ends and moving
# that boundary would invalidate the recording corpus.
SPD_REWARD_FREE_STEP_COST_FACTOR=0.5

# --- reward: the rest -------------------------------------------------------
SPD_REWARD_MAX_HP_REWARD=0.5

# Per talent point spent. BIG - most of a floor's 25. Levelling pays 2 per level and that is right: a
# level gives +1 attack, +1 defence and a little max HP and happens whether the agent plays well or
# not. A point is a permanent choice about WHICH gains to take, and the options are not remotely equal
# (LiquidAgility 2 is infinite evasion; VeteranIntuition 2 identifies your armour on the spot).
#
# Reachable since Action.TALENT landed: env.TalentPicker enumerates what the game would offer and the
SPD_REWARD_TALENT_REWARD=400.0
SPD_REWARD_GOLD_REWARD=0.05
SPD_REWARD_CURRICULUM_PROGRESS=0.0

# --- reward: the terms that were Java literals ------------------------------------------
#
# All twenty of these were numbers written into RewardModel. They are the same values they always
# were; what changed is that a run can be told what they are and a config file can change them.
SPD_REWARD_IDENTIFIED_REWARD=0.5
SPD_REWARD_CURSE_EQUIPPED_PENALTY=-5.0
SPD_REWARD_CURSE_REMOVED_REWARD=1.5
SPD_REWARD_EQUIP_TOO_STRONG_PENALTY=-2.0
SPD_REWARD_CURED_DEBUFF_REWARD=1.5
SPD_REWARD_EATEN_EARLY_PENALTY=-1.0
SPD_REWARD_MENU_NOOP_PENALTY=-1.0
SPD_REWARD_LEVEL_UP_REWARD=2.0
SPD_REWARD_STRENGTH_GAIN_REWARD=1.0
SPD_REWARD_GOLD_LOST_FACTOR=2.0
SPD_REWARD_ITEM_VALUE_BAG=3.0
SPD_REWARD_ITEM_VALUE_EQUIP_BASE=1.0
SPD_REWARD_ITEM_VALUE_EQUIP_LEVEL=0.5
SPD_REWARD_ITEM_VALUE_OTHER=0.5
SPD_REWARD_BOSS_SLAIN_FACTOR=2.0
SPD_REWARD_MAX_HP_GAIN_CAP=10.0
#
# Depths over which the dense-to-sparse fade runs: 1.0 up to the start depth, 0.0 from the end
# depth, smoothstepped strictly between. Nothing has passed floor 2 yet, so the scale has been 1.0
# on every episode so far.
SPD_REWARD_CURRICULUM_FADE_START_DEPTH=3
SPD_REWARD_CURRICULUM_FADE_END_DEPTH=10

# --- learning ---------------------------------------------------------------
SPD_RL_LEARNING_RATE=0.0003
SPD_RL_GAMMA=0.99
SPD_RL_GAE_LAMBDA=0.95
SPD_RL_CLIP_EPSILON=0.2
SPD_RL_ENTROPY_COEFFICIENT=0.01
SPD_RL_EPOCHS=2
SPD_RL_MINIBATCH_SIZE=32
SPD_RL_SAMPLE_RATE=0.05
SPD_RL_MAX_SAMPLED_PER_EPISODE=2048
SPD_RL_MAX_SAMPLES_PER_GENERATION=8192
SPD_RL_STALL_SECONDS=180
# 1 is the serial path, exactly, and is what `parallelcheck` compares against. Measured 8.98 -> 2.73
# ms/sample at 1 -> 4 threads; the curve flattens past 4 because the gradient reduction is 14.3 MB
# per thread per minibatch. Raise this to 4 on a machine whose cores are not already all running
# workers.
SPD_RL_UPDATE_THREADS=1

# --- episode limits ---------------------------------------------------------
SPD_ENV_TURN_LIMIT_PER_FLOOR=1500
SPD_ENV_TURN_LIMIT_TOTAL=40000
SPD_ENV_STALL_LIMIT=120
# A second stall guard, for the loop the first cannot see: stall_limit counts steps where the hero did
# not move, so one move resets it, and a free-action loop interleaves the two. Measured: 502 of 1215
# steps advancing no engine time was 41% of that episode's cost.
SPD_ENV_FREE_STEP_BUDGET=250
SPD_ENV_ACTOR_STEP_LIMIT=20000
SPD_ENV_MAX_SLOTS=96
SPD_ENV_GRID_WIDTH=48
SPD_ENV_GRID_HEIGHT=48

# --- vision and items -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Clamp on hero.viewDistance when building the observation grid. Vision buffs (Light, Magical
# Sight) are honoured, as they are for a human player, and mimics stay visible outside the field
# of view once seen, which keeps the agent's information set equal to a player's rather than
# strictly smaller.
SPD_ENV_MAX_VIEW_DISTANCE=12
SPD_ENV_HONOUR_VISION_BUFFS=true
SPD_ENV_MIMICS_VISIBLE_OUT_OF_FOG=true

# Allow equipping from the inventory pane. Recorded in every replay header, because a recorded slot
# index means something different when this is false.
SPD_ENV_ALLOW_EQUIPPING=true

# Shop and blacksmith dialogs, and the alchemy pot. Both are now reachable: Action.ALCHEMY opens a
# sub-mode over Recipe.findRecipe without going through AlchemyScene.
SPD_ENV_ALLOW_TRADING=true
SPD_ENV_ALLOW_ALCHEMY=true

# Let the game's save code write to disk. Off by default: a rollout performs millions of turns'
# worth of incidental saves and none of them are ever read back.
SPD_ENV_PERSIST_SAVES=false
# --- the recurrent gradient ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consecutive steps per backpropagated run. ONE is a length-one truncation: nothing crosses a timestep
# and the LSTM's hidden-to-hidden weights learn nothing the trunk could not.
SPD_RL_CHUNK_LENGTH=16
SPD_RL_TAIL_STEPS=20

# --- the critic ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The reward function is priced for the agent, not the optimiser: returns sit in the thousands, so an
# unnormalised critic lost to global clipping on the shared trunk and took the policy's update with it.
SPD_RL_NORMALISE_VALUES=true
SPD_RL_VALUE_NORM_MOMENTUM=0.01
SPD_RL_VALUE_LOSS_COEFFICIENT=0.5
SPD_RL_VALUE_GRADIENT_CLIP=10.0
SPD_RL_HUBER_VALUES=true

# --- the optimiser ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPD_RL_MAX_GRAD_NORM=0.5
SPD_RL_ADAM_BETA1=0.9
SPD_RL_ADAM_BETA2=0.999
SPD_RL_ADAM_EPS=1.0E-8

# --- the run ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Zero is a real setting, not "off": it is what makes two runs of one configuration comparable.
SPD_TRAIN_RANDOM_SEED_RATE=0.10
SPD_TRAIN_CHECKPOINT_EVERY=25
SPD_TRAIN_RECORD_EVERY=1

# --- pipes and worker JVMs --------------------------------------------------------------------
SPD_IPC_PIPE_BUFFER_BYTES=1048576
SPD_IPC_PUSH_CHUNK_BYTES=32768
# Writes of the above retried before the push is refused. A pipe that fails eight times is a pipe
# that is gone.
SPD_TRAINER_PUSH_RETRIES=8
SPD_WORKER_HEAP_MIN=256m
SPD_WORKER_HEAP_MAX=1536m
SPD_WORKER_GC_PAUSE_MS=200

# --- dialogs -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPD_ENV_DIALOG_AGE_SECONDS=0.2
